server bound to a port
headers, as the handler receives them:
  Extension x-custom: value
  Warning 199 note
  Via 1.1 proxy
  UserAgent test/1.0
  Upgrade [h2c; websocket]
  TransferEncoding
  Trailer Expires
  TE trailers
  Referer proto=http host=host port=8080 path=p
  Referer proto=/local/path host= port=None path=
  Referer proto=http host= port=None path=/host:8080/p/q
  ProxyAuthorization Basic def
  CacheControl NoCache
  MaxForwards 0
  MaxForwards 3
  IfRange "e4"
  IfNoneMatch "e3"
  IfMatch [e1; e2]
  IfMatch *
  Host unknown-host None
  Host localhost 8080
  Host localhost:8080 None
  Host localhost None
  From someone@example.org
  Expect
  Cookies [a=1; b=x y; c=]
  ContentDisposition form-data [name="f"; filename="a b.txt"]
  ContentLength 0
  ContentType text/html [charset=utf-8; q=1]
  Connection close
  CacheControl Extension0 a b c
  CacheControl Extension2 community uci
  CacheControl Extension1 private
  CacheControl OnlyIfCached
  CacheControl NoTransform
  CacheControl MinFresh 7
  CacheControl MaxStale 5
  CacheControl MaxAge 60
  CacheControl Extension1 max-age=60
  CacheControl NoStore
  CacheControl NoCache
  Authorization Basic abc
  AcceptLanguage en
  AcceptEncoding gzip
  AcceptCharset utf-8
  Accept text/html
reply: HTTP/1.0 200 OK
multipart:
  two fields               [a=one; b=two\r\nlines]
  empty value              [e=]
  name unquoted            [u=v]
  no name                  raises Failure("parse_post_body: form-data has no name")
  not form-data            raises Failure("parse_post_body: bad Content-Disposition: attachment")
  no disposition           raises Failure("parse_post_body: part has no Content-Disposition")
  no boundary in the body  []
  no boundary parameter    raises Failure("parse_post_body: boundary is not defined")
  urlencoded               [x=1; y=a b&; z=]
  other type               raises Failure("parse_post_body: unknown content type: text/plain")
